1
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:12,100
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:32,867
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:35,600
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,133 --> 00:00:41,500
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:44,500
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:45,600
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:46,767
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:47,433 --> 00:00:48,667
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:51,633
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,767 --> 00:00:53,800
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:56,133
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:57,033 --> 00:00:58,167
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,167 --> 00:01:00,733
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,433 --> 00:01:02,800
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,633 --> 00:01:06,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:08,667 --> 00:01:09,833
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:12,133
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:12,133 --> 00:01:13,533
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,533 --> 00:01:14,833
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,067 --> 00:01:22,533
<i> One million pesos!</i>

21
00:01:22,533 --> 00:01:24,900
<i>I deserve to eat
something delicious.</i>

22
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:26,567
<i> Because now I'm rich.</i>

23
00:01:26,567 --> 00:01:27,967
<i>It feels so good!
Oh, the scent!</i>

24
00:01:27,967 --> 00:01:29,200
<i> The files in front of you</i>

25
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:30,500
<i>are everything we have
on the Victor Zafra case.</i>

26
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:32,033
How about the whole Zafra clan?

27
00:01:32,033 --> 00:01:33,500
They're the ones who killed Sam.

28
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:34,667
<i> From this day forward,</i>

29
00:01:34,667 --> 00:01:36,533
<i>this will officially
be your case.</i>

30
00:01:36,533 --> 00:01:37,900
Find the people who killed Sam.

31
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:39,633
<i>The people he fought
last night came back.</i>

32
00:01:39,633 --> 00:01:40,867
<i>You're not getting out
of here alive!</i>

33
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:42,500
<i>- Enough!
- Gabo, don't!</i>

34
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:44,033
<i>Don't take the law
into your own hands.</i>

35
00:01:44,033 --> 00:01:45,933
<i>- You promised, didn't you?
- I'm sorry.</i>

36
00:01:45,933 --> 00:01:46,900
<i> Long live Gabo!</i>

37
00:01:46,900 --> 00:01:47,933
<i>- Long live!
- Long live!</i>

38
00:01:47,933 --> 00:01:50,500
[ALL]
<i> Gabo! Gabo! Gabo! Gabo!</i>

39
00:01:50,767 --> 00:01:51,733
[GRUNTS]

40
00:01:52,867 --> 00:01:55,833
- [PANTING]
- [MEN COUGHING]

41
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,467
[GROANS]

42
00:01:58,733 --> 00:01:59,733
[LINE RINGS]

43
00:01:59,733 --> 00:02:01,000
Boss!

44
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,900
We're at a disadvantage here
in Ginintuang Lupa.

45
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:04,400
Someone interfered!

46
00:02:06,733 --> 00:02:07,700
Okay, boss.

47
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,100
- Let's go!
- [MAN] Come on!

48
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:11,433
[MEN GRUNTING]

49
00:02:11,433 --> 00:02:12,400
Hurry!

50
00:02:15,933 --> 00:02:20,467
Boss, our men
from Ginintuang Lupa called.

51
00:02:20,467 --> 00:02:21,500
Which men?

52
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:23,933
Samantha Jacinto is gone, right?

53
00:02:23,933 --> 00:02:25,533
What are they still doing there?

54
00:02:25,900 --> 00:02:27,100
What happened?

55
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:29,533
Apparently, the residents there
ganged up on them.

56
00:02:29,533 --> 00:02:30,433
Ganged up on them?

57
00:02:30,767 --> 00:02:32,100
What are they? Useless?

58
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:34,067
They're Safra's men.
How did they get ganged up on?

59
00:02:34,567 --> 00:02:36,533
They have guns!

60
00:02:37,067 --> 00:02:38,567
If they got ganged up on,

61
00:02:39,567 --> 00:02:40,933
it can only mean one thing.

62
00:02:41,867 --> 00:02:43,067
What is it, Pa?

63
00:02:43,067 --> 00:02:45,567
They're blocking our men.

64
00:02:45,567 --> 00:02:47,200
They're ready to fight.

65
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:49,533
So our men can't get in.

66
00:02:50,267 --> 00:02:52,733
They're protecting someone.

67
00:02:52,733 --> 00:02:54,967
They're hiding something,
keeping a secret.

68
00:02:54,967 --> 00:03:01,900
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

69
00:03:01,900 --> 00:03:04,267
Wooh! [CHUCKLES]

70
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:05,800
Oh...

71
00:03:06,667 --> 00:03:08,900
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

72
00:03:08,900 --> 00:03:09,900
There's someone.

73
00:03:19,967 --> 00:03:26,633
[INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES]

74
00:03:26,667 --> 00:03:28,300
[EXHALES] Don't disappear, okay?

75
00:03:28,300 --> 00:03:32,600
Don't disappear.
I'll come back for you.

76
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:34,000
Just stay here.

77
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:39,333
[INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES]

78
00:03:39,333 --> 00:03:40,567
[SIGHS]

79
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,633
I'll come back for you later.

80
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:46,133
Mama just has somewhere to go.

81
00:03:46,133 --> 00:03:49,833
And you, come here.

82
00:03:49,833 --> 00:03:51,967
I'll get some money.

83
00:03:59,833 --> 00:04:02,000
Django is from Ginintuang Lupa,
right?

84
00:04:03,233 --> 00:04:04,867
Let's just talk to him, boss.

85
00:04:04,867 --> 00:04:06,033
No.

86
00:04:06,033 --> 00:04:07,867
We're not asking Django
for help.

87
00:04:07,867 --> 00:04:09,200
Let's attack them, boss.

88
00:04:09,733 --> 00:04:12,600
Find out who attacked our men.

89
00:04:13,233 --> 00:04:14,900
And don't you dare come back

90
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:17,633
until you find out
who's behind this.

91
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:19,367
Yes, boss.

92
00:04:19,367 --> 00:04:20,833
We'll take care of it.

93
00:04:23,833 --> 00:04:24,967
[GUNS CLICKING]

94
00:04:24,967 --> 00:04:27,667
You want us to find the ones
who attacked us?

95
00:04:28,067 --> 00:04:30,367
Don't waste your time on that.

96
00:04:30,367 --> 00:04:33,000
Then what, Ma?!
What am I supposed to tell Papa?

97
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,933
That I couldn't even
finish this?

98
00:04:34,933 --> 00:04:39,000
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

99
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:42,867
Son, if you want your father
to trust you,

100
00:04:42,867 --> 00:04:45,600
you need to make
sound decisions.

101
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:47,733
Stop wasting precious time

102
00:04:47,733 --> 00:04:50,167
on worthless endeavors
like this.

103
00:04:50,167 --> 00:04:55,700
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

104
00:04:55,700 --> 00:04:58,067
Boss, we can still leave.

105
00:04:58,067 --> 00:05:00,033
If you want.

106
00:05:00,033 --> 00:05:04,667
Are we just going to let those
who fought us go?

107
00:05:06,267 --> 00:05:07,633
For now.

108
00:05:07,633 --> 00:05:09,067
But their day will come.

109
00:05:10,933 --> 00:05:13,133
I won't forget what they did.

110
00:05:13,133 --> 00:05:18,267
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

111
00:05:18,267 --> 00:05:25,233
[ALL]
Gabo! Gabo! Gabo! Gabo!

112
00:05:30,300 --> 00:05:31,767
Hey! Hey! Hey!

113
00:05:31,767 --> 00:05:33,067
- [ALL] Gabo! Gabo! Gabo!
- Shh!

114
00:05:33,067 --> 00:05:34,300
[BETCHAY] What happened?

115
00:05:34,333 --> 00:05:37,433
What happened?
Why does it look like--

116
00:05:37,433 --> 00:05:39,433
Why do you all look like
you came from a war?

117
00:05:39,433 --> 00:05:40,767
You wouldn't believe it,
Betchay.

118
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:43,000
Gabo's enemies came back again.

119
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,300
- Men he fought the other day.
- [BETHCAY] Huh?!

120
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:46,467
- Really?!
- They were no match for us.

121
00:05:46,467 --> 00:05:47,433
They were nothing!

122
00:05:47,433 --> 00:05:50,033
[GUSHING]

123
00:05:50,900 --> 00:05:51,967
[SIGHS DEEPLY]
Oh no.

124
00:05:52,267 --> 00:05:56,167
Gabo, are you okay? Hmm?

125
00:05:56,167 --> 00:06:01,100
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

126
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:02,900
Ah, I'm fine, Mama Betchay.

127
00:06:03,967 --> 00:06:06,133
[SIGHS] Thank God.

128
00:06:06,133 --> 00:06:07,967
- Oh, wow!
- Really?

129
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:10,800
[BETCHAY] I knew
you could handle it, Gabo.

130
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:13,267
You've been getting into
fistfights since you were a kid.

131
00:06:13,267 --> 00:06:15,433
You're already a master at it!

132
00:06:17,033 --> 00:06:19,833
Miss Betchay, for the
first time, you're so positive!

133
00:06:19,833 --> 00:06:21,800
[CROWD LAUGHING]

134
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:24,167
What a miracle! No sermon?

135
00:06:24,833 --> 00:06:26,367
[DABOY] Nice! No shouting today!

136
00:06:26,367 --> 00:06:28,167
No fighting, either.

137
00:06:28,167 --> 00:06:31,000
I woke up in a good mood!
You want me to get mad instead?

138
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:32,267
- Oh, no!
- No! No!

139
00:06:32,267 --> 00:06:39,267
[ALL] Betchay! Betchay! Betchay!

140
00:06:40,433 --> 00:06:41,800
Oh, wait, wait.

141
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:43,867
Why are you leaving
pretty early?

142
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:45,267
Where are you going?

143
00:06:46,167 --> 00:06:47,167
There.

144
00:06:48,033 --> 00:06:49,767
I just have somewhere to go.

145
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:53,000
That's why I'm leaving
early today.

146
00:06:53,867 --> 00:06:57,500
[BETCHAY] <i> I have to make sure
</i> they don't get into my room.

147
00:07:01,500 --> 00:07:02,967
Oh, right!

148
00:07:02,967 --> 00:07:04,833
Don't go into my room for now.

149
00:07:04,833 --> 00:07:07,200
I saw a huge snake.

150
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:08,200
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

151
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:10,500
[BETCHAY] It was this big!
This big!

152
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:14,333
But don't worry because
I already killed it.

153
00:07:14,367 --> 00:07:16,533
I already killed the snake.
But, um...

154
00:07:16,533 --> 00:07:19,000
Just be careful because
it might have a family.

155
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,767
It came from the roof.

156
00:07:20,767 --> 00:07:23,533
So don't go in there for now.

157
00:07:23,533 --> 00:07:24,867
[INHALES]

158
00:07:25,267 --> 00:07:26,300
I'll get going.

159
00:07:26,767 --> 00:07:28,133
Go ahead and eat.

160
00:07:28,433 --> 00:07:29,567
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

161
00:07:29,567 --> 00:07:31,000
What happened to her?

162
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,400
Her mood seems different today.

163
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:34,567
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

164
00:07:34,567 --> 00:07:36,000
Don't get your hopes up!

165
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,067
- She said there's a snake.
- Maybe it bit her.

166
00:07:39,433 --> 00:07:41,200
Don't contradict Mama Betchay.

167
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:45,233
Maybe she just woke up
in a good mood.

168
00:07:45,233 --> 00:07:46,333
- Yeah, right.
- Okay.

169
00:07:46,333 --> 00:07:47,533
- That's right.
- Okay.

170
00:07:47,567 --> 00:07:49,867
- I don't believe it.
- Just go along with it.

171
00:07:51,367 --> 00:07:54,033
People of Ginintuang Lupa,
listen up!

172
00:07:56,033 --> 00:07:58,267
Thank you so, so much
for all your help!

173
00:07:58,267 --> 00:08:00,000
Especially Mister Babot
and the others.

174
00:08:01,433 --> 00:08:02,900
And to my friends.

175
00:08:04,867 --> 00:08:06,933
To protect our community.

176
00:08:07,567 --> 00:08:09,067
If it weren't for all of you,

177
00:08:10,367 --> 00:08:13,933
we wouldn't have defeated
and driven away our enemies.

178
00:08:13,933 --> 00:08:16,133
So let's give ourselves
a round of applause.

179
00:08:16,133 --> 00:08:23,067
[CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

180
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:25,267
But it's not over yet.

181
00:08:25,833 --> 00:08:28,967
We still need to guard
every corner

182
00:08:28,967 --> 00:08:30,500
and alley in our community.

183
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:33,267
So if our enemies come back,

184
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:35,967
we'll always be ready.

185
00:08:35,967 --> 00:08:37,100
Do we understand each other?

186
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:38,467
[ALL] Yes!

187
00:08:38,467 --> 00:08:39,833
Anyone who goes against Gabo...

188
00:08:39,833 --> 00:08:41,067
- Will be crushed!
- Will be crushed!

189
00:08:41,067 --> 00:08:42,100
Anyone who goes against Gabo...

190
00:08:42,100 --> 00:08:43,133
- Will be crushed!
- Will be crushed!

191
00:08:43,133 --> 00:08:44,300
Anyone who goes against Gabo...

192
00:08:44,300 --> 00:08:45,633
- Will be crushed!
- Will be crushed!

193
00:08:45,633 --> 00:08:48,900
[LIGHTHEARTED MUSIC PLAYING]

194
00:08:52,100 --> 00:08:55,767
[PHONE RINGING]

195
00:08:56,833 --> 00:08:58,100
[SIGHS]

196
00:08:59,933 --> 00:09:02,100
This better be good news, Pia.

197
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:04,800
NCIA is now targeting you.

198
00:09:04,800 --> 00:09:06,333
What else is new?

199
00:09:06,333 --> 00:09:08,933
Should I be flattered
that both NLEA

200
00:09:08,933 --> 00:09:11,500
and NCIA are after us?

201
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:14,000
[PIA] <i> It's serious
</i> this time around.

202
00:09:14,867 --> 00:09:16,667
Because of what happened to Sam,

203
00:09:16,967 --> 00:09:18,933
they're really coming after you.

204
00:09:18,933 --> 00:09:23,067
They're going to file a case
against you.

205
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:26,900
To hold you accountable
for Jacinto's death.

206
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:29,500
They don't learn, do they?

207
00:09:30,800 --> 00:09:32,833
Isn't it enough

208
00:09:33,067 --> 00:09:36,867
<i>that we've already taken down
a number of your agents</i>

209
00:09:36,867 --> 00:09:39,500
and even that Samantha Jacinto?

210
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:42,033
What?

211
00:09:42,133 --> 00:09:45,800
Does the NCIA want to have
all of you killed?

212
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:48,467
All I can say
is prepare yourself

213
00:09:48,467 --> 00:09:49,867
and be ready, ma'am.

214
00:09:49,867 --> 00:09:51,533
[DEBORAH] <i> They are the ones
</i> who should be prepared.

215
00:09:51,533 --> 00:09:54,000
Or should I say... your group?

216
00:09:56,467 --> 00:09:57,867
What are you planning?

217
00:09:57,867 --> 00:10:02,500
Looks like they're forgetting
just who the Zafras really are.

218
00:10:02,533 --> 00:10:04,500
I will remind them...

219
00:10:05,667 --> 00:10:07,533
who we are.

220
00:10:07,533 --> 00:10:11,567
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

221
00:10:11,567 --> 00:10:12,567
[DOOR OPENS]

222
00:10:12,567 --> 00:10:13,900
- Sir.
- Here, Castor.

223
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:15,867
I've already signed this.
You can take it already.

224
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:17,667
I appreciate it, sir.

225
00:10:17,667 --> 00:10:19,600
Oh, by the way, I'm planning
on doing something.

226
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:20,800
What is it, sir?

227
00:10:21,033 --> 00:10:24,100
I have a restaurant reservation
tonight.

228
00:10:24,100 --> 00:10:25,900
We'll have a small gathering.

229
00:10:25,900 --> 00:10:27,500
To remember...

230
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:29,600
Sam.

231
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:31,567
Sir, that's a great idea.

232
00:10:31,767 --> 00:10:33,933
I'm sure the whole team
will be happy with that.

233
00:10:33,933 --> 00:10:35,900
Good. Tell the whole team
about it

234
00:10:35,933 --> 00:10:38,700
and tell Pia to visit my office.

235
00:10:38,700 --> 00:10:42,133
Since the Jacinto family
didn't let us visit Sam's wake,

236
00:10:42,133 --> 00:10:44,567
her NCIA family
will remember her

237
00:10:44,567 --> 00:10:47,067
in their own way instead.

238
00:10:47,567 --> 00:10:49,467
Yes, sir. I'll be on it.

239
00:10:49,467 --> 00:10:53,800
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

240
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:57,100
So Sir Delgado wants to do
a tribute dinner?

241
00:10:57,100 --> 00:10:59,233
He said it won't be
a formal event.

242
00:10:59,233 --> 00:11:01,233
According to him it's just
a small gathering.

243
00:11:01,233 --> 00:11:03,133
You know what, I think
that's a great idea, Castor.

244
00:11:03,133 --> 00:11:05,767
I really want to pay my respects
to my fellow comrade.

245
00:11:05,767 --> 00:11:07,900
We're going to do this
for ourselves.

246
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:09,467
To grieve with each other.

247
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:13,733
But we also shouldn't forget
what we have to do for Sam.

248
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,600
She's right.

249
00:11:15,600 --> 00:11:19,667
The most important of all
is to get justice for Sam.

250
00:11:19,667 --> 00:11:21,833
You know, we'll never forget
about that.

251
00:11:21,833 --> 00:11:24,933
With me leading
this investigation,

252
00:11:25,167 --> 00:11:27,067
I'm sure that we'll succeed.

253
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:29,700
But for now,

254
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,067
we grieve.

255
00:11:31,633 --> 00:11:33,900
We'll let our broken hearts
bleed.

256
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:34,967
[SIGHS SHARPLY]

257
00:11:34,967 --> 00:11:37,567
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

258
00:11:37,567 --> 00:11:38,900
[SEBASTIAN SIGHS]

259
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:41,600
- [FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]
- [STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

260
00:11:41,633 --> 00:11:42,633
[PIA] Sir.

261
00:11:42,833 --> 00:11:44,967
- You called for me?
- [DELGADO] Yes.

262
00:11:44,967 --> 00:11:49,100
Pia, we will have
a tribute dinner for Sam.

263
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:51,667
And everybody will be there.

264
00:11:51,667 --> 00:11:54,133
We didn't do that
for other fallen agents.

265
00:11:54,800 --> 00:11:57,100
Hold on, is Ma'am Pia invited?

266
00:11:57,500 --> 00:11:59,700
Yeah, well,
it's what sir wanted.

267
00:11:59,700 --> 00:12:01,200
What's her use in being there?

268
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:04,000
We're already feeling bad
and she'll make it worse?

269
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,633
Maybe we should just give
Ma'am Pia a chance.

270
00:12:06,633 --> 00:12:08,533
We know she's strict.

271
00:12:08,533 --> 00:12:10,667
But you know what,
she's probably not that bad.

272
00:12:10,833 --> 00:12:13,200
And we're doing this
for Ma'am Sam.

273
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:15,300
Then no matter what
Sir Delgado wants to do,

274
00:12:15,333 --> 00:12:16,833
let's just give it to him.

275
00:12:17,167 --> 00:12:19,200
Plus, who knows?

276
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:22,867
She may have learned her lesson
with what she did to Sam.

277
00:12:22,867 --> 00:12:27,167
Well, no one's got our backs
but us, right?

278
00:12:27,167 --> 00:12:30,067
Fine. The dinner isn't
about be about me anyway.

279
00:12:30,067 --> 00:12:32,033
But if I hear her talk nonsense

280
00:12:32,033 --> 00:12:33,833
then we'll be the dinner's
highlight, trust.

281
00:12:34,833 --> 00:12:35,833
[SCOFFS]

282
00:12:35,833 --> 00:12:37,167
However...

283
00:12:37,633 --> 00:12:39,000
that's a great idea, sir.

284
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:41,867
Jacinto was a special agent.

285
00:12:42,033 --> 00:12:43,500
That's why...

286
00:12:44,067 --> 00:12:45,667
it's only right for her
to be recognized.

287
00:12:45,667 --> 00:12:47,700
I'll be expecting you
to be there.

288
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,167
- Hmm.
- [DELGADO] Pia.

289
00:12:49,167 --> 00:12:52,267
Unless you're busy
with your work.

290
00:12:52,267 --> 00:12:56,067
Sir, even if her comrades
believe

291
00:12:56,067 --> 00:12:59,700
that I was too uptight
with Jacinto,

292
00:12:59,700 --> 00:13:01,567
she's still a loss for me.

293
00:13:02,733 --> 00:13:04,933
So... I'll be there.

294
00:13:04,933 --> 00:13:06,333
[INHALES SHARPLY]

295
00:13:06,333 --> 00:13:07,700
To grieve.

296
00:13:07,700 --> 00:13:08,833
Thank you.

297
00:13:10,767 --> 00:13:11,933
Excuse me, sir.

298
00:13:11,933 --> 00:13:15,900
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING, FADES]

299
00:13:15,900 --> 00:13:19,900
Gabo... can I talk to them too?

300
00:13:20,567 --> 00:13:22,033
It's just about
what we should change

301
00:13:22,067 --> 00:13:24,167
here in Ginintuang Lupa
while they're still here.

302
00:13:25,867 --> 00:13:27,033
Sure thing, my love.

303
00:13:27,033 --> 00:13:28,600
Is there something
you wish to say?

304
00:13:28,900 --> 00:13:29,900
Can I?

305
00:13:31,967 --> 00:13:33,167
Everyone!

306
00:13:34,200 --> 00:13:36,233
Gloria has something important
to say.

307
00:13:36,233 --> 00:13:38,700
[DIDAY] Alright, listen up!
Silence!

308
00:13:38,700 --> 00:13:40,267
My buddy has something to say.

309
00:13:40,267 --> 00:13:41,733
- Listen up!
- [SAM GIGGLES]

310
00:13:41,733 --> 00:13:43,100
Thanks, buddy.

311
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:44,733
Uh...

312
00:13:44,733 --> 00:13:46,867
Everyone, first of all,

313
00:13:47,067 --> 00:13:50,767
thank you so much
for saving our community.

314
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:56,033
But I wish we could avoid
getting into fights and chaos.

315
00:13:56,733 --> 00:14:00,033
Showing our love for our town

316
00:14:00,933 --> 00:14:04,133
can be through
maintaining cleanliness

317
00:14:04,133 --> 00:14:06,867
and order in our community.

318
00:14:07,933 --> 00:14:10,367
It doesn't just manifest
with the use of our fists.

319
00:14:11,167 --> 00:14:12,733
It could be through brooms too.

320
00:14:13,767 --> 00:14:14,933
Or old sacks of rice.

321
00:14:14,933 --> 00:14:16,900
From our very own hands.

322
00:14:18,633 --> 00:14:19,800
Uh...

323
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:24,633
We can start with scraps
that could be dangerous.

324
00:14:24,633 --> 00:14:25,900
Let's get rid of them.

325
00:14:26,267 --> 00:14:29,800
Those electrical wires
tangled everywhere,

326
00:14:29,833 --> 00:14:31,300
let's just dispose of them.

327
00:14:31,300 --> 00:14:34,933
Let's all start segregating
our wastes.

328
00:14:35,433 --> 00:14:39,833
Let's separate the biodegradable
from the non-biodegradable.

329
00:14:40,767 --> 00:14:43,967
Uh, as for items
that still look decent,

330
00:14:43,967 --> 00:14:45,467
we can sell them
at the junk shop.

331
00:14:45,467 --> 00:14:47,667
We can repair them too.

332
00:14:47,667 --> 00:14:50,933
We can make handicrafts too,
we could sell them.

333
00:14:50,933 --> 00:14:52,333
- [SIGHS]
- [WHISPERING] Hey.

334
00:14:53,133 --> 00:14:55,333
Stop doing that. You'll end up
looking like that forever.

335
00:14:55,333 --> 00:14:56,933
- Mind your own!
- She'll end up cross-eyed.

336
00:14:56,933 --> 00:14:58,967
- Hey, listen properly!
- You listen yourself!

337
00:14:58,967 --> 00:15:03,433
Uh, I wish we can stop
engaging with fights

338
00:15:03,467 --> 00:15:05,000
and gossiping from now on.

339
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:07,200
Ow! That must've hurt!

340
00:15:07,200 --> 00:15:09,133
- I'll make sure to do that!
- [LAUGHTER]

341
00:15:09,133 --> 00:15:11,100
- You're amazing, buddy!
- [LAUGHING]

342
00:15:11,733 --> 00:15:14,033
So if you are willing
to sacrifice your life

343
00:15:14,033 --> 00:15:15,700
for Ginintuang Lupa,

344
00:15:16,167 --> 00:15:20,733
I hope you can also live
for Ginintuang Lupa.

345
00:15:20,733 --> 00:15:23,233
[ALL CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

346
00:15:23,233 --> 00:15:24,867
Django, stop that.

347
00:15:24,867 --> 00:15:26,767
[SAM] Let's start cleaning up!

348
00:15:27,200 --> 00:15:28,733
[CHATTER]

349
00:15:28,733 --> 00:15:31,233
Gloria, you can run
as the town captain now!

350
00:15:31,233 --> 00:15:34,833
- All right!
- [ALL EXCLAIMING]

351
00:15:34,867 --> 00:15:39,400
[CHANTING] Gloria! Gloria!

352
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:40,367
Love,

353
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:42,700
your words were beautiful.

354
00:15:43,733 --> 00:15:46,033
Sam, thank you so much
for the...

355
00:15:46,033 --> 00:15:48,167
love and care you have for...

356
00:15:48,433 --> 00:15:51,733
my family and my fellow
townspeople.

357
00:15:51,733 --> 00:15:56,033
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

358
00:15:56,033 --> 00:15:57,967
I keep loving you more each day.

359
00:15:59,033 --> 00:16:00,833
Because your heart
is made of gold.

360
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:05,867
[GABO] You know...

361
00:16:06,433 --> 00:16:08,367
even I am impressed by Gloria.

362
00:16:08,400 --> 00:16:10,200
I never expected that...

363
00:16:10,433 --> 00:16:12,867
she'll love and care
for all of us.

364
00:16:12,967 --> 00:16:15,933
That's why I hope that her words

365
00:16:15,933 --> 00:16:18,567
remain in our hearts and minds

366
00:16:18,567 --> 00:16:20,933
because those are what will help
our town.

367
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:22,933
As well as our families.

368
00:16:23,133 --> 00:16:24,467
Are we clear?

369
00:16:24,467 --> 00:16:25,933
- [BONG] Of course, Gabo!
- [ALL APPLAUDING]

370
00:16:25,933 --> 00:16:30,933
- [BONG] Love live, Gloria!
- [ALL] Long live!

371
00:16:30,933 --> 00:16:33,900
- [BONG] Love live, Gloria!
- [ALL] Long live!

372
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:38,267
- Long live, Gloria!
- [ALL] Long live!

373
00:16:38,267 --> 00:16:41,533
[ALL APPLAUDING, CHEERING]

374
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:45,933
So all it takes is Gloria
to soften this tough guy up!

375
00:16:45,933 --> 00:16:48,433
- [ALL EXCLAIMING]
- What?

376
00:16:48,433 --> 00:16:50,433
- Long live, Gloria!
- I love you so much.

377
00:16:50,433 --> 00:16:57,100
- Long live, Gloria!
- [ALL] Long live!

378
00:16:57,100 --> 00:17:03,967
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
BY JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

379
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:10,433
What the hell is going on?

380
00:17:10,733 --> 00:17:13,200
Are you going to attack
the NCIA?

381
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:15,300
They're planning an attack.

382
00:17:15,333 --> 00:17:17,133
We're just getting
ahead of them.

383
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:20,333
Kill or be killed.

384
00:17:20,333 --> 00:17:21,600
[SIGHS SHARPLY]

385
00:17:22,867 --> 00:17:25,267
NCIA headquarters
is heavily guarded.

386
00:17:25,267 --> 00:17:29,467
Security is tight,
and they have eyes everywhere.

387
00:17:29,467 --> 00:17:31,100
And most importantly,

388
00:17:31,100 --> 00:17:34,667
they are fully equipped
to take you on.

389
00:17:34,667 --> 00:17:36,500
Pia's there.

390
00:17:36,500 --> 00:17:38,967
She'll keep us posted.

391
00:17:38,967 --> 00:17:41,633
She'll provide us intel

392
00:17:41,633 --> 00:17:45,000
when the time
is right to attack.

393
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:46,533
We don't need her, Pa.

394
00:17:46,533 --> 00:17:49,633
We're moving now
to take them down quicker!

395
00:17:51,133 --> 00:17:53,200
All right, gear up.

396
00:17:54,067 --> 00:17:55,133
Let's go!

397
00:17:55,133 --> 00:18:01,467
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

398
00:18:01,467 --> 00:18:06,367
Your son is so compulsive.

399
00:18:06,367 --> 00:18:08,533
[ENGINES REVVING]

400
00:18:08,533 --> 00:18:11,367
[TIRES SCREECH]

401
00:18:11,367 --> 00:18:13,200
- Arturo.
- Sir?

402
00:18:13,200 --> 00:18:15,000
Call Django.

403
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:16,067
Yes, sir.

404
00:18:16,067 --> 00:18:17,967
What are your orders for him?

405
00:18:17,967 --> 00:18:20,367
I want him to attack the NCIA.

406
00:18:20,467 --> 00:18:21,467
No.

407
00:18:22,500 --> 00:18:24,367
Lucas will handle this.

408
00:18:24,367 --> 00:18:27,933
Your son is being stubborn.

409
00:18:27,933 --> 00:18:30,567
He's not being strategic
with this attack.

410
00:18:30,567 --> 00:18:34,667
Django, on the other hand,
plans every move carefully.

411
00:18:34,667 --> 00:18:37,367
We don't need to
involve Django

412
00:18:37,367 --> 00:18:39,367
in all our problems.

413
00:18:39,367 --> 00:18:42,067
He proved himself, didn't he?

414
00:18:42,067 --> 00:18:44,233
One successful mission

415
00:18:44,233 --> 00:18:47,567
does not earn him
a seat in this family.

416
00:18:47,567 --> 00:18:50,233
Well, I'm not giving him one.

417
00:18:50,233 --> 00:18:51,400
I know.

418
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:55,033
But with every job
we give him,

419
00:18:55,067 --> 00:18:56,600
he gets deeper into our family.

420
00:18:56,600 --> 00:18:59,133
He's learning
how we operate,

421
00:18:59,133 --> 00:19:01,067
how our business operates,

422
00:19:01,067 --> 00:19:02,733
and who our enemies are.

423
00:19:02,733 --> 00:19:04,700
Django's a stranger.

424
00:19:04,700 --> 00:19:08,467
We can't trust him.

425
00:19:08,467 --> 00:19:14,133
We should be very, very careful
who we'll let into our world.

426
00:19:14,133 --> 00:19:17,967
Especially those
who are dying to get into it.

427
00:19:17,967 --> 00:19:21,267
- [EXHALES HEAVILY]
- [GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

428
00:19:21,267 --> 00:19:22,567
- Arturo.
- Sir?

429
00:19:24,100 --> 00:19:26,033
Provide backup for Lucas.

430
00:19:26,033 --> 00:19:27,667
Yes, sir.
Ma'am.

431
00:19:31,267 --> 00:19:32,733
- Guys, come on.
- [GUN COCKS]

432
00:19:32,733 --> 00:19:35,133
We need to go.
Chop, chop.

433
00:19:35,133 --> 00:19:37,633
Karen, did you ring Rallos?

434
00:19:37,633 --> 00:19:39,267
Is he coming?

435
00:19:39,267 --> 00:19:41,000
I did, but he said
he can't make it.

436
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:42,633
They're still at Laguna.

437
00:19:42,633 --> 00:19:45,233
You could've convinced him.
He'd do anything for you.

438
00:19:45,233 --> 00:19:47,300
- Hmph!
- [CHUCKLES] Too bad.

439
00:19:47,300 --> 00:19:49,633
It would've been better
if Team Alpha were complete.

440
00:19:49,633 --> 00:19:51,100
Correction,

441
00:19:51,100 --> 00:19:53,233
Team Alpha will
never be complete again.

442
00:19:53,233 --> 00:19:56,100
We'll always be down a member
with Sam gone.

443
00:19:56,100 --> 00:19:59,067
But she'll forever be
a part of our team.

444
00:19:59,067 --> 00:20:04,300
Guys, I'm heading over
to the resto.

445
00:20:04,333 --> 00:20:06,767
Who needs a ride?
Come on!

446
00:20:08,133 --> 00:20:09,300
- Um...
- Team?

447
00:20:09,300 --> 00:20:11,367
- Hmm?
- Who wants a ride...

448
00:20:11,367 --> 00:20:12,500
with Ma'am Pia?

449
00:20:12,500 --> 00:20:13,533
Hmm?

450
00:20:13,533 --> 00:20:20,600
[COMICAL MUSIC PLAYING]

451
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:23,167
Uh, ma'am?

452
00:20:23,167 --> 00:20:24,467
Go ahead.

453
00:20:24,467 --> 00:20:26,767
We'll follow in a bit.

454
00:20:26,767 --> 00:20:28,267
See you there.

455
00:20:31,367 --> 00:20:32,567
Drive safely.

456
00:20:37,533 --> 00:20:38,867
[MUSIC TURNS DARK]

457
00:20:38,867 --> 00:20:43,700
[PIA]    I'll give you something
to mourn over.

458
00:20:49,167 --> 00:20:51,133
[DIDAY] All right, folks!

459
00:20:51,133 --> 00:20:53,133
What are ya'll waiting for?

460
00:20:53,133 --> 00:20:54,367
Go home!

461
00:20:54,367 --> 00:20:56,667
Do something useful there!

462
00:20:56,667 --> 00:20:58,300
- [CHUCKLES]
- Oh, wait a minute.

463
00:20:58,300 --> 00:21:00,467
Remember what Gloria said?

464
00:21:00,467 --> 00:21:02,333
No more gossip!

465
00:21:02,333 --> 00:21:04,700
Unless you want
your tongues cut off!

466
00:21:04,700 --> 00:21:09,700
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]
- Go on!

467
00:21:09,733 --> 00:21:13,333
- Go!
- Now, wait a minute! Come on!

468
00:21:13,333 --> 00:21:15,300
- Move it.
- We'll clean up, Gabo.

469
00:21:16,500 --> 00:21:18,700
[TEKLA] Wait!
I have something to say!

470
00:21:18,700 --> 00:21:20,833
- Folks, hear me out!
- [TOLITS] Just tell us.

471
00:21:20,833 --> 00:21:24,700
Oh my goodness, Gloria,
you continue to impress me.

472
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:28,267
In the short time you've spent
here in Ginintuang Lupa,

473
00:21:28,267 --> 00:21:33,167
you've done more good

474
00:21:33,167 --> 00:21:36,700
than the people who
are running this place.

475
00:21:36,700 --> 00:21:37,700
- Yes.
- That's right.

476
00:21:37,700 --> 00:21:40,200
- It's amazing.
- Mm-hmm.

477
00:21:40,200 --> 00:21:42,667
You are one of a kind, Gloria.

478
00:21:42,700 --> 00:21:48,200
[GABO] That's why
I love my wife so much.

479
00:21:48,200 --> 00:21:49,633
[CHUCKLES]

480
00:21:49,633 --> 00:21:54,067
It doesn't matter how long
you've been in a community.

481
00:21:54,067 --> 00:21:58,200
Home is where the heart is.

482
00:21:58,200 --> 00:22:00,400
So you do whatever
it takes for it.

483
00:22:00,400 --> 00:22:05,133
But Ginintuang Lupa has
something other places don't.

484
00:22:05,133 --> 00:22:07,367
You have compassion
for one another.

485
00:22:07,367 --> 00:22:11,100
[RUDY] Yes, Gloria.
Spoken like a true leader.

486
00:22:11,100 --> 00:22:14,600
[GABO] Pa, she's a woman
of action, not just words.

487
00:22:14,600 --> 00:22:16,567
[MAMENG CHUCKLES]
All right, now...

488
00:22:16,600 --> 00:22:18,900
I'm going to cook.
You must be hungry.

489
00:22:18,900 --> 00:22:21,467
You went through
a lot today.

490
00:22:21,467 --> 00:22:23,233
[RUDY] Whip up something good.

491
00:22:23,233 --> 00:22:24,467
- [MAMENG] Excuse me?
- Oh.

492
00:22:24,467 --> 00:22:28,233
- My food is always good!
- You're right. Sorry.

493
00:22:28,233 --> 00:22:29,400
- Watch it.
- All right, Rudy.

494
00:22:29,400 --> 00:22:30,833
- All right.
- Gabo, I'll go back to work.

495
00:22:30,833 --> 00:22:32,800
All right.
Come on.

496
00:22:32,800 --> 00:22:36,133
Oh, wait. What if
the snake is still there?

497
00:22:36,133 --> 00:22:37,567
What if Betchay's right?

498
00:22:37,567 --> 00:22:39,800
Oh, don't mind her.

499
00:22:39,800 --> 00:22:41,267
She was just imagining it.

500
00:22:41,267 --> 00:22:43,233
- All right. Come with me then.
- Go on.

501
00:22:43,233 --> 00:22:46,133
- What about the snake?!
- What snake? Hmm?

502
00:22:46,133 --> 00:22:48,300
- Go on, you coward.
- Keep walking.

503
00:22:48,300 --> 00:22:50,733
Man up. It's just a snake.

504
00:22:50,767 --> 00:22:57,267
[WHIMSICAL MUSIC PLAYING]

505
00:22:57,267 --> 00:22:58,500
Oh my.

506
00:23:03,133 --> 00:23:04,267
Mm, that's good.

507
00:23:05,833 --> 00:23:07,433
[WAITER] Your mango shake.

508
00:23:07,433 --> 00:23:08,733
- Perfect timing.
- [GLASS CLINKS]

509
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:13,500
So this is what it's like to eat

510
00:23:13,500 --> 00:23:16,567
without worrying about the bill.

511
00:23:21,300 --> 00:23:24,267
I could get used to this.
[SCOFFS]

512
00:23:24,300 --> 00:23:25,400
Delicious!

513
00:23:25,400 --> 00:23:26,633
Mm-hmm.

514
00:23:26,633 --> 00:23:33,267
[WHIMSICAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

515
00:23:42,800 --> 00:23:45,333
Two unfortunate souls.

516
00:23:46,467 --> 00:23:48,267
Been there...

517
00:23:49,367 --> 00:23:51,800
Done that! [SCOFFS]

518
00:23:51,800 --> 00:23:53,500
I'm going to enjoy this!

519
00:23:53,500 --> 00:23:55,867
I deserve this! [LAUGHS]

520
00:23:55,900 --> 00:23:58,833
Miss, where are
the imported items?

521
00:23:58,833 --> 00:24:00,400
The imported section
is over there.

522
00:24:00,400 --> 00:24:03,333
This is the local section.
It's cheaper here.

523
00:24:03,333 --> 00:24:05,833
I'm not looking for cheap;
I want to buy imported goods.

524
00:24:05,833 --> 00:24:08,200
I have money.
I have lots of money!

525
00:24:08,200 --> 00:24:10,900
I can even buy you
if I want to.

526
00:24:14,833 --> 00:24:16,667
These look good.
That's the stuff!

527
00:24:16,667 --> 00:24:19,267
Uh, miss, where are
your local merchandise?

528
00:24:19,267 --> 00:24:21,600
- Right there, ma'am.
- Ah...

529
00:24:21,600 --> 00:24:23,433
I thought you wanted
imported stuff?

530
00:24:23,433 --> 00:24:25,433
Yes, for myself.

531
00:24:25,433 --> 00:24:26,867
The local stuff
is for my family.

532
00:24:26,867 --> 00:24:31,367
Those people have
no taste and no money!

533
00:24:31,467 --> 00:24:32,733
Like you.

534
00:24:34,933 --> 00:24:36,933
Are you sure
you want gold nails, ma'am?

535
00:24:36,933 --> 00:24:38,433
I think baby pink
would suit you better.

536
00:24:38,433 --> 00:24:40,933
Did I ask for your opinion?

537
00:24:40,933 --> 00:24:43,600
I want gold because
it reflects my current status.

538
00:24:43,600 --> 00:24:47,067
Madam got
the full package today.

539
00:24:47,067 --> 00:24:49,533
She got her nails done,
her legs waxed,

540
00:24:49,600 --> 00:24:51,867
her brows fixed,
and her hair treated!

541
00:24:51,867 --> 00:24:54,733
Madam,
what's the special occasion?

542
00:24:54,733 --> 00:24:58,900
Can't a lady pamper herself?!

543
00:24:58,900 --> 00:25:02,900
You know, I know why
you're chatting me up.

544
00:25:02,933 --> 00:25:06,933
You want to get a big tip.

545
00:25:06,933 --> 00:25:09,767
Y'all don't make enough
money, do you?

546
00:25:09,767 --> 00:25:11,767
Stop-- Ouch! Stop it!

547
00:25:11,833 --> 00:25:15,467
Cut the chitchat
and do your jobs!

548
00:25:15,467 --> 00:25:16,800
I'm sorry, ma'am.

549
00:25:16,800 --> 00:25:18,967
Focus on that.
Go!

550
00:25:18,967 --> 00:25:21,500
You call that a massage?!

551
00:25:21,500 --> 00:25:22,067
More pressure!
Harder!

552
00:25:24,067 --> 00:25:26,467
In fact, what Gloria said
made sense.

553
00:25:27,400 --> 00:25:31,300
Hmm! When did you learn
the meaning of the word sense?

554
00:25:31,300 --> 00:25:32,333
Since yesterday.

555
00:25:32,333 --> 00:25:34,100
- [LAUGHS]
- Does it make sense?

556
00:25:34,100 --> 00:25:36,100
- Funny.
- Gloria's really good, right?

557
00:25:36,133 --> 00:25:37,433
[BONG] Gloria, the best!

558
00:25:37,433 --> 00:25:40,000
- Yes!
- What she said is right.

559
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:42,167
If we want to be respected,

560
00:25:42,167 --> 00:25:44,600
we should respect the place too.

561
00:25:45,267 --> 00:25:46,300
That's right!

562
00:25:46,300 --> 00:25:49,333
Like the saying,
there's money in trash!

563
00:25:49,333 --> 00:25:52,033
What about Daboy? Looks like
trash but doesn't have money?

564
00:25:52,033 --> 00:25:53,633
[LAUGHTER]

565
00:25:53,633 --> 00:25:56,167
You know, you're too impressed!

566
00:25:56,167 --> 00:25:58,133
Just because
she offered to clean,

567
00:25:58,133 --> 00:26:00,600
she thinks she's some
kind of saint now!

568
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:03,033
Okay! Looks like Tekla
is getting jealous!

569
00:26:03,033 --> 00:26:04,167
[LAUGHTER]

570
00:26:04,167 --> 00:26:06,167
You, be quiet! You look like
a piggy bank!

571
00:26:06,500 --> 00:26:08,167
You're too harsh on Daboy!

572
00:26:08,167 --> 00:26:09,600
He didn't say anything wrong.

573
00:26:09,633 --> 00:26:10,967
Didn't say anything wrong?!

574
00:26:10,967 --> 00:26:12,333
That girl is really
an attention-seeker!

575
00:26:12,333 --> 00:26:13,500
[BONG] Attention-seeker?

576
00:26:13,500 --> 00:26:15,233
[IPE] It's okay to be
an attention-seeker,

577
00:26:15,233 --> 00:26:16,467
instead of being meddlesome!

578
00:26:16,467 --> 00:26:18,200
Oh, I see. I see.

579
00:26:18,200 --> 00:26:20,533
Hey, you might have forgotten.

580
00:26:20,533 --> 00:26:22,367
That woman is part of the NCIA!

581
00:26:22,367 --> 00:26:24,167
NCIA!

582
00:26:24,167 --> 00:26:25,533
Why are you like that?!

583
00:26:25,533 --> 00:26:27,400
She might bump her head and
suddenly remember everything!

584
00:26:27,400 --> 00:26:29,533
- Then, what?
- Let's hit her head again!

585
00:26:29,533 --> 00:26:31,500
- Right, right, right.
- Your solution's nonsense!

586
00:26:31,500 --> 00:26:33,367
If her memory comes back,

587
00:26:33,367 --> 00:26:36,067
she'll surely not forget
the good times we had together.

588
00:26:36,067 --> 00:26:38,067
- I doubt it!
- This is good for us!

589
00:26:38,067 --> 00:26:40,033
So she'll know that
we are good people, right?

590
00:26:40,033 --> 00:26:42,533
You're too weak-willed!

591
00:26:43,167 --> 00:26:45,333
Tekla, we're not weak-willed.

592
00:26:45,333 --> 00:26:47,067
You're just too hard.

593
00:26:47,067 --> 00:26:49,367
Oh, am I? Do you want me
to sack all of you?

594
00:26:49,367 --> 00:26:50,733
That's too much!

595
00:26:50,733 --> 00:26:52,167
Is that true?

596
00:26:52,167 --> 00:26:53,267
[SCREAMS] That's true!

597
00:26:53,267 --> 00:26:54,733
- Daddy!
- Damn you! Let's go!

598
00:26:54,733 --> 00:26:56,700
- Let's go! Damn all of you!
- It's getting hot!

599
00:26:56,700 --> 00:26:58,200
- Let's go somewhere cool!
- Come on!

600
00:26:59,700 --> 00:27:00,900
Uhm...

601
00:27:02,267 --> 00:27:03,367
Love,

602
00:27:04,700 --> 00:27:07,067
thank you so much

603
00:27:07,067 --> 00:27:09,967
for your love and care for us.

604
00:27:10,533 --> 00:27:13,633
Especially for my family
and friends.

605
00:27:16,067 --> 00:27:17,400
I'm happy to do that.

606
00:27:18,133 --> 00:27:19,433
You know, I hope that

607
00:27:20,200 --> 00:27:21,533
soon,

608
00:27:21,533 --> 00:27:23,367
everything you said
will come true.

609
00:27:24,267 --> 00:27:26,267
I hope this place
will change for the better.

610
00:27:28,100 --> 00:27:29,600
You have been
a great help to us.

611
00:27:30,467 --> 00:27:32,433
Thank you for having
a good heart.

612
00:27:32,433 --> 00:27:36,367
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

613
00:27:36,367 --> 00:27:38,033
I love you so much, Gloria.

614
00:27:39,633 --> 00:27:41,167
So much.

615
00:27:44,567 --> 00:27:51,533
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
BY JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

616
00:28:05,900 --> 00:28:07,800
He's like the director of NCIA.

617
00:28:07,800 --> 00:28:09,000
<i>They're the ones
who captured my brother.</i>

618
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:11,667
<i>They will also file a case
against my family.</i>

619
00:28:11,667 --> 00:28:14,933
<i>They are having a reunion
with Samantha Jacinto in hell.</i>

620
00:28:14,933 --> 00:28:17,233
<i> Ricardo Jacinto ordered them</i>

621
00:28:17,233 --> 00:28:19,767
<i>to get ownership
of our land here!</i>

622
00:28:19,767 --> 00:28:22,900
<i>If Gabo didn't come,
the people there will be dead.</i>

623
00:28:22,933 --> 00:28:25,300
<i>You know that I'm not going
to let anyone in our area</i>

624
00:28:25,300 --> 00:28:26,700
<i> get hurt or be put in danger.</i>

625
00:28:26,700 --> 00:28:29,133
<i>This is the first time
I've seen a man like this.</i>

626
00:28:29,133 --> 00:28:31,767
<i>He's willing to sacrifice
his life for others.</i>

627
00:28:31,767 --> 00:28:33,933
<i>They want us to
have a lot of children.</i>

628
00:28:33,933 --> 00:28:36,833
<i>Perhaps we can start
making a lot of babies later.</i>

629
00:28:36,833 --> 00:28:38,533
<i> It was a gift.</i>

630
00:28:38,533 --> 00:28:40,133
<i> Don't think about them.</i>

631
00:28:40,133 --> 00:28:42,667
<i> Victor. That Victor.</i>

632
00:28:42,667 --> 00:28:44,667
<i> Victor Safra?</i>

633
00:28:44,667 --> 00:28:45,667
What's your connection with him?

634
00:28:45,667 --> 00:28:47,567
What do you have to do with him?
